<title>USA: National Insurance buys back shares.</title>
<headline>National Insurance buys back shares.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH SAN FRANCISCO, Calif. 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Insurance Group on Tuesday said it repurchased 705,300 shares of common stock for approximately $5 million.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said the shares were acquired through a private transaction with an institutional investor at a price of $7 per share.</p>
<p>Upon settlement on September 20, the shares repurchased will be returned to the status of authorized, but unissued shares of the company, leaving the number of common shares outstanding to 3,996,897.</p>
</text>
